# Dotfiles — Configuration as Code

> Declarative, Stow-managed dotfiles with multi-machine support.
> Consolidates 3 legacy repos into a single Stow-managed codebase.

## Documentation Map

This repo has three layers of documentation — read the one that matches your question:

| You're asking... | Read |
|---|---|
| "How do I install/use/troubleshoot this?" | **This README** |
| "What are the rules for working in this repo as an AI agent?" | `AGENT.md` |
| "What's the target architecture, and why?" | `docs/src/Dotfiles GitOps Architecture — Source of Truth` |
| "What's shipped vs. planned, and in what order?" | `docs/src/PRD` |
| "How did the design get here?" | `docs/src/Architecture-Proposal` → `-Audit` → `-Evaluations_beta` → `-Evaluations_validation`, in that order |

This README documents **current, working reality**. The `docs/src/` chain documents the target architecture and the reasoning behind it — treat anything there describing `dotctl`, host manifests, or a reconciler as the plan, not the present.

